      "text": "To determine the volume of the inscribed sphere, we first need to find its radius. Since the sphere is inscribed in the cube, the diameter of the sphere is equal to the edge length of the cube. Given that the edge length of the cube is 6 inches, the diameter of the sphere is also 6 inches, and the radius \\( r \\) of the sphere is half of that, which is \\( \\frac{6}{2} = 3 \\) inches.\n\nThe formula for the volume \\( V \\) of a sphere is given by:\n\\[\nV = \\frac{4}{3} \\pi r^3\n\\]\nSubstituting the radius \\( r = 3 \\) inches into the formula, we get:\n\\[\nV = \\frac{4}{3} \\pi (3)^3\n\\]\nFirst, we calculate \\( 3^3 \\):\n\\[\n3^3 = 27\n\\]\nThus, the volume becomes:\n\\[\nV = \\frac{4}{3} \\pi \\times 27\n\\]\nNow, we perform the multiplication:\n\\[\nV = \\frac{4 \\times 27}{3} \\pi = \\frac{108}{3} \\pi = 36 \\pi\n\\]\nTherefore, the volume of the inscribed sphere is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{36\\pi}\n\\]",
